="Shadow",name="Darkness",r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=40,l2=40,tree="Shadow",name="Shadowform",r1=1,r2=1,max=1},{l1=41,l2=45,tree="Discipline",name=S[442],r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=46,l2=47,tree="Discipline",name="Martyrdom",r1=1,r2=2,max=2},{l1=48,l2=50,tree="Discipline",name=S[339],r1=1,r2=3,max=5},{l1=51,l2=53,tree="Discipline",name="Meditation",r1=1,r2=3,max=3},{l1=54,l2=54,tree="Discipline",name="Inner Focus",r1=1,r2=1,max=1},{l1=55,l2=58,tree="Shadow",name=S[582],r1=2,r2=5,max=5},{l1=59,l2=60,tree="Shadow",name=S[592],r1=1,r2=2,max=5}},blocks={{t="anchor",id="overview"},{t="p",s="eyebrow",x=S[413]},{t="h1",x="Shadow",sub=S[481]},{t="p",s="lede",x="Damage over time from range: Shadow Word: Pain, Devouring Plague and Mind Blast, Mind Flay between them, and Shadowform at 40 to halve your Shadow mana costs."},{t="pills",list={S[521],"Solo questing and ranged damage",S[448]}},{t="anchor",id="journey"},{t="kicker",x=S[553]},{t="h2",x=S[355]},{t="p",x="These stages follow the talent order below. Shadow has the least downtime for solo questing; mana is tight until Shadowform at 40."},{t="p",s="level",x="10–24 · Spirit Tap and reach"},{t="p",x="Spirit Tap 5/5 at 14 doubles your Spirit after a kill and lets 50% of your mana regeneration continue while casting. Improved Shadow Word: Pain adds 6 seconds to the damage-over-time spell, Shadow Reach adds 20% range to your Shadow spells, and Blackout 5/5 by 24 gives Shadow damage a 10% chance to stun."},{t="p",s="level",x="25–39 · Embrace, Flay and Contagion"},{t="p",x="Vampiric Embrace at 25 heals your party for 20% of your Shadow damage, Shadow Weaving 3/3 by 28 stacks up to 10% more Shadow damage from you, Mind Flay at 29 replaces Smite as your filler, and Silence at 30 is your interrupt. Devouring Contagion 2/2 (31–32) halves Devouring Plague’s cost and spreads it on death, Improved Mind Flay 2/2 (33–34) ramps each tick, and Darkness 5/5 by 39 adds 10% Shadow damage."},{t="p",s="level",x="40–60 · Shadowform and support"},{t="p",x="Shadowform at 40: 10% more Shadow damage, half-cost Shadow spells, double the critical damage bonus and 15% less physical damage taken, but no healing spells while it is active. Twin Disciplines, Martyrdom, Mental Strength, Meditation and Inner Focus fill 41–54, Shadow Focus reaches 5/5 at 58 for 5% Shadow hit, and Dark Inspiration finishes the build at 60."},{t="anchor",id="talents"},{t="kicker",x=S[393]},{t="h2",x=S[521]},{t="p",x=S[60]},{t="widget",w="talents"},{t="h4",s="summary",x=S[421]},{t="widget",w="ranks"},{t="h4",s="summary",x=S[375]},{t="p",x="Spend one point per level in each range. Unlisted talents stay at zero. This order runs to 60 and has been checked for totals, maximum ranks, tier gates and prerequisites."},{t="widget",w="order"},{t="p",s="notice",x="The build takes Blackout for its stuns; take Shadow Focus instead if you miss many casts in dungeons or on higher-level enemies. Another option is a wand-based Discipline build for 10–39 (Meditation first) with a respec at 40; this page follows the Shadow build from 10. Shadow Weaving in Forever only boosts your own Shadow damage."},{t="anchor",id="stats"},{t="kicker",x=S[482]},{t="h2",x=S[405]},{t="p",x="Shadow wants hit until the cap, then spell power and critical strike. Mana is tight until Shadowform, so Spirit helps while you level."},{t="h3",x=S[538]},{t="stat",i=1,b=S[578],x=S[516]},{t="stat",i=2,b="Spirit",x=S[459]},{t="stat",i=3,b="Intellect",x="mana pool"},{t="stat",i=4,b="Stamina",x=""},{t="p",s="small",x="From level 36, pick wands with spell damage, Intellect and Spirit."},{t="h3",x="At level 60"},{t="stat",i=1,b="Hit chance",x="to 17%"},{t="stat",i=2,b="Spell power",x=S[516]},{t="stat",i=3,b=S[523],x=""},{t="stat",i=4,b="Spell penetration",x=""},{t="stat",i=5,b="Spirit",x=""},{t="p",s="small",x="Shadow Focus gives 5% hit, so you need 12% from gear. Some estimates put crit above spell power."},{t="p",s="notice",x="Spell hit cap: 17% against raid bosses (level 63), 4% against enemies of your own level. The level 60 list is an early estimate: the beta stopped at level 30, so expect changes once endgame gear is known. A big upgrade in a lower stat can still beat a small one in a higher stat."},{t="anchor",id="combat"},{t="kicker",x=S[406]},{t="h2",x=S[432]},{t="p",x="Treat this as a priority list, not a fixed loop. Mind Flay arrives at 29 in this order, Shadow Word: Death at 32 and Shadowform at 40."},{t="h4",x=S[466]},{t="p",x="Keep Power Word: Fortitude and Inner Fire up. From 40, enter Shadowform before the pull and stay in it; leave it only to heal yourself."},{t="h4",x="Open"},{t="p",x="Shield yourself if the enemy will reach you (skip it in groups), then pull with Mind Blast. Before Mind Flay, open with Smite and follow with Mind Blast."},{t="h4",x="Apply damage over time"},{t="p",x="Shadow Word: Pain, then Devouring Plague (every Priest learns it at 20). With Devouring Contagion, the Plague spreads to two nearby enemies when the target dies."},{t="h4",x="Mind Flay and wand"},{t="p",x="Channel Mind Flay between spells and let it finish when safe: Improved Mind Flay makes each tick stronger than the last. Before 36 or when low on mana, finish with your wand instead."},{t="h4",x="Finish"},{t="p",x="From 32, Shadow Word: Death finishes an enemy it will kill; if the target survives, you take damage equal to 30% of your maximum health."},{t="h4",x="Control and recovery"},{t="p",x="Silence interrupts dangerous casts, Psychic Scream (14) buys room but can pull more enemies, and Vampiric Embrace heals you and your party. Spirit Tap and Dark Inspiration speed up mana recovery after kills."},{t="abil",names={"Shadowform","Mind Blast","Shadow Word: Pain","Devouring Plague","Mind Flay","Shadow Word: Death",S[515],"Silence"}},{t="h3",x=S[467]},{t="p",x="Leveling priority for Shadow: spell damage, critical strike, hit, then Intellect, Stamina and mana per 5 seconds. Hit becomes more important at 60 and against higher-level enemies."},{t="p",x="Use wands until Mind Flay takes over in your mid-30s; wand shots do not scale with spell damage. Gravestone Scepter (Blackfathom Deeps) adds Shadow damage and Spirit, which keep it useful after you stop shooting."},{t="h3",x=S[422]},{t="p",x="You do not need a healing spec to heal leveling dungeons: leave Shadowform and heal with Renew, Power Word: Shield and downranked Heal. After 40 healing gets harder, so consider a second healing spec at 50–60."},{t="p",x="In groups, Vampiric Embrace keeps the party topped up and Dark Inspiration raises their Spirit. Pulling several enemies with Shadow Word: Pain is possible but drains Inner Fire charges and mana quickly."},{t="anchor",id="macros"},{t="kicker",x=S[483]},{t="h2",x=S[340]},{t="p",x=S[52]},{t="p",s="notice",x=S[53]},{t="macro",n=S[389],x=S[86],code=S[146]},{t="macro",n=S[524],x=S[105],code=S[196]},{t="macro",n=S[460],x=S[117],code=S[171]},{t="macro",n=S[356],x=S[97],code=S[136]},{t="macro",n=S[433],x=S[113],code=S[162]},{t="macro",n=S[468],x=S[161],code=S[175]},{t="macro",n=S[348],x=S[152],code=S[390]},{t="macro",n=S[434],x=S[184],code=S[195]},{t="macro",n=S[461],x=S[192],code=S[289]},{t="macro",n="Mouseover Silence",x="Stops your current cast and silences the enemy under your pointer or your target, interrupting its spell.",code="#showtooltip Silence\n/stopcasting\n/cast [@mouseover,harm,nodead][harm,nodead] Silence"},{t="macro",n="Mind Flay without restarting",x="Repeated presses do not restart the channel, so you keep the stronger later ticks from Improved Mind Flay.",code="#showtooltip Mind Flay\n/cast [nochanneling:Mind Flay] Mind Flay"},{t="macro",n="Shadow Word: Death finisher",x="Use only when it will kill the target; if it survives, you take damage equal to 30% of your maximum health.",code="#showtooltip Shadow Word: Death\n/cast [harm,nodead] Shadow Word: Death"},{t="macro",n="Leave Shadowform and heal",x="Cancels Shadowform, then Flash Heals the ally under your pointer or yourself. Recast Shadowform after the fight. Not tested in game.",code="#showtooltip Flash Heal\n/cancelaura Shadowform\n/cast [@mouseover,help,nodead][@player] Flash Heal"},{t="p",s="small",x=S[226]},{t="anchor",id="dungeons"},{t="kicker",x=S[525]},{t="h2",x=S[376]},{t="p",x=S[55]},{t="widget",w="rarity"},{t="p",s="notice",x=S[56]},{t="p",s="notice",x=S[29]},{t="widget",w="loot"},{t="anchor",id="professions"},{t="kicker",x=S[407]},{t="h2",x=S[373]},{t="p",x=S[66]},{t="widget",w="prof"},{t="anchor",id="crafting"},{t="kicker",x=S[423]},{t="h2",x=S[357]},{t="p",x=S[25]},{t="widget",w="craft"},{t="anchor",id="questgear"},{t="kicker",x=S[408]},{t="h2",x=S[332]},{t="p",x=S[28]},{t="widget",w="quest"},{t="anchor",id=S[388]},{t="kicker",x=S[526]},{t="h2",x="Your notes"},{t="widget",w="notes"},{t="p",s="small",x=S[87]}}}},dungeons={{n=S[321],lr="13–18",st=S[123],no=S[16],ba=true,ra={ck=S[166],r={},t={},no={S[39],S[167],S[31]}}},{n=S[285],lr="13–18",st=S[123],no=S[16],ba=true,ra={ck=S[166],r={},t={},no={S[39],S[167],S[31]}}},{n=S[165],lr="15–20",st=S[123],no=S[16],ba=true,ra={ck=S[166],r={{n="Lordaeron Captain",st=S[80],no=S[95],it={}}},t={},no={S[91],S[41],S[31]}}},{n=S[212],lr="17–24",st=S[123],no=S[16],ba=true,ra={ck=S[166],r={{n=S[444],st=S[80],no=S[95],it={}}},t={},no={S[91],S[167],S[31]}}},{n=S[214],lr="17–26",st=S[123],no=S[16],ba=true,ra={ck=S[166],r={{n="Miner Johnson",st=S[80],no=S[245],it={}}},t={},no={S[91],S[41],S[31]}}},{n=S[228],lr="22–30",st=S[123],no=S[16],ba=true,ra={ck=S[166],r={{n="Deathsworn Captain",st=S[80],no=S[95],it={}},{n="Gefell",st=S[80],no=S[95],it={}},{n="Gemela",st=S[80],no=S[95],it={}}},t={},no={S[91],S[41],S[31]}}},{n=S[385],lr="24–32",st=S[123],no=S[16],ba=true,ra={ck=S[166],r={{n="Bruegal Ironknuckle",st=S[80],no=S[245],it={}}},t={},no={S[91],S[41],S[31]}}},{n=S[139],lr="24–32",st=S[123],no=S[16],ba=true,ra={ck=S[166],r={},t={},no={S[39],S[41],S[31]}}},{n=S[200],lr="26–31",st=S[123],no=S[16],ba=true,ra={ck=S[166],r={},t={},no={S[39],S[167],S[31]}}},{n=S[129],lr="28–33",st=S[123],no=S[16],b